WEBVTT

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.730
<i>Tonegawa Yukio. The number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.990
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.240
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.080
<i>Tonegawa completes President Hyoudou's 
diabolically unreasonable demands with ease.</i>

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.710
<i>And in order to do that, he needs the 
support of his subordinates, the men in black.</i>

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.500
<i>To that end, he must always 
be ready for action</i>

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.010
<i>as he guides and supervises his employees.</i>

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.760
<i>That's what middle management is all about!</i>

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.340
<i>However, it's no simple task.</i>

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.850
<i>Some of his workers fail 
to produce. Some run wild.</i>

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.850
<i>Some even manage to cause trouble 
after leaving their position!</i>

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.350
<i>These men in black may all look the same,</i>

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.610
<i>but they all have their own quirks that 
make each uniquely hard to handle.</i>

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.860
<i>Indeed! This is the story of an 
executive in charge of many workers,</i>

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.110
<i>as he struggles between his 
employer, the president,</i>

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.330
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:05.040
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about a lone man.</i>

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.680
Excuse me. Can I talk to you for a second?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.620
Oh, Nakata. What is it?

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.060
Could you take a look at this?

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.030
That's the Teiai official Twitter account.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.280
Tweets               Following               Followers

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.280
<b>Tweets                    Tweets & Replies</b>

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.280
Teiai Official

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.280
The official account for Teiai Finance! We're here 
to give you fun information on events and campaigns, 
plus a few laughs along the way.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.280
Another sunny and warm day in Tokyo. {some emojis i'm not sure on how to recreate} (Zzz...)

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.040
Come to think of it, you run this, don't you?

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.280
Yes...

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:40.030
Only 136 followers?

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.760
And only 18 tweets...

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.540
I-I'm sorry, sir!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:49.880
I just have no idea what an account 
for Teiai should be tweeting about!

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.410
Come on, the contents of 
the tweets don't matter.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.470
Listen here. The important 
thing here is frequency.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.390
Even if it's a single tweet each 
day, you need to keep it up.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.120
That'll gradually net you more followers...

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:09.970
Hey.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.980
Who to follow?

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.980
<b>Account to Destroy Teiai

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:14.980
What's this "Account to Destroy 
Teiai" under "Who to follow"?

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.650
Oh, that's some kind of hate 
account that popped up recently.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.000
"Teiai is like coffee with 
no milk or sugar: black."

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.710
"I thought I saw a black hole 
once, but it was just Teiai."

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.130
This is asinine.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:37.050
It's probably just someone in deep 
debt with a grudge against Teiai...

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.130
<b>Tweets      Following      Followers</b>

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.150
Hey! Nakata!

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.890
Look at this! The hate account's 
got more followers than you!

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.850
Hey, you're right!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.250
Forget it! This is too much for you to handle!

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.510
Starting today, I'll do it!

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.030
I'm going to be the guy behind 
the official Twitter account!

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:08.120
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:08.120
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.910
<i>Agenda 21
<b>

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:34.490
I'm not sure this is something 
you need to handle personally...</b></i>

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.210
Fool!

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.730
Nowadays it's not just major businesses!

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.960
Even heads of state make use of Twitter!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.130
You can't underestimate the 
influence that social media has!

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.310
If you think about it,

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.530
this is the kind of job that someone 
higher on the ladder should have.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.230
I was wrong to have you do it in the first place.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.100
Yes, sir.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.110
<i>And so it begins...</i>

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:05.890
<i>Tonegawa's life as the man behind 
the official Teiai Twitter.</i>

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.450
Good weather today in Tokyo once again!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.700
Looks like rain today!
Be sure to bring an umbrella!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.240
<i>80% of his tweets</i>

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.730
<i>consist of notes on the weather.</i>

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.750
Strong winds today!
There's been an unexpected typhoon warning!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.750
It'd be unthinkably outrageous to go out...
without an umbrella today!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.630
It looks like there's a lot of pollen in the air today!
Better safe than sorry when it comes to allergies...
If you need help covering the expenses,
contact Teiai Finance!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.630
<i>Along with the occasional plug for Teiai,</i>

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:25.380
Special notice!
If you follow the Teiai Official account
and retweet this message, you'll be entered
for a chance to receive a Teiai clear file and
a prepaid card! #TeiaiCampaign

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.070
<i>and occasional follow & retweet campaigns</i>

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.490
<i>for a chance to win Teiai merchandise.</i>

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.220
<i>With each passing day, the tweets add up.</i>

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:39.270
<i>The follower count has gone up, 
but it's still not where I want it.</i>

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.530
<i>Not only that, but most of the new followers</i>

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.700
<b>Yoshio</b>@yso-

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:51.160
<b>Yoshio</b>@yso-

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.480
<i>are just trash that have accounts exclusively</i>

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:50.240
<b>Yoshio</b>@yso-

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.160
<i>for entering follow & retweet giveaways.</i>

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.160
<b>Yoshio</b>@yso-

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.620
<i>There's no point in doing things this way.</i>

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.670
<i>Huh? Someone liked one of the tweets.</i>

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.920
Yamazaki@ZAKIYAMA_TEIAI liked your tweet

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.920
<b>TeiaiOfficial</b>@TEIAI_JAPAN
Special notice! If you follow the Teiai Official account and retweet...

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.920
Yamazaki@ZAKIYAMA_TEIAI liked your tweet

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.920
<b>TeiaiOfficial</b>@TEIAI_JAPAN
Eyes open! There's a super moon tonight!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:05.640
<i>Yamazaki... I don't need your pity, damn it.</i>

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:12.660
<i>The Account to Destroy Teiai 
has 598 followers?!</i>

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:17.350
<i>They've widened the gap even further!</i>

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:21.310
I see.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.800
Whoever's behind this 
knows what they're doing.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:27.030
I think you might just 
be outmatched here, sir.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.700
That can't be...

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.030
Look here.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.930
At a glance, it seems like all this account 
is doing is spamming criticism...

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:36.580
#WriteAPoemWithOnlyTWords

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.580
Teiai's a sweatshop

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.580
But there's more to it.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:42.580
Teiai's violent black heart

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.370
Like these animated gifs of cute cats!

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:46.090
Not only that, but they're using really 
efficient fodder to get likes...

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.540
Like original fan art of popular anime,

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.590
I hope Yuinyan never even learns that sweatshops exist

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.870
#DescribeYourselfInOneWord

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.420
and going aggressively after any 
hashtags that are trending high.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:59.600
#WriteAPoemWithOnlyTWords
Trust no one  Their money's blood
Total sham  Teiai's dirty  tom yum goong

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.950
Not to mention how they pin any 
tweet that ends up being buzzworthy.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.160
B-Buzzwhaty?

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:06.360
Meanwhile, your tweets, Tonegawa-sensei...

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.950
Today's weather is clear with afternoon clouds.
Probably a good idea to bring an umbrella when you go out.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:14.370
A crane and a turtle...

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.610
are 80% long-winded weather posts,

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:14.370
along with occasional boring 
pictures of the clouds.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.730
This is hard for me to say, sir,

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:20.750
but when it comes to Twitter, 
you and this hate account are like

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.960
a child and an adult.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.010
The difference is that apparent.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.010
<b>Psst...</b>

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:31.220
If it's all right with you, 
I can take over from—

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.260
Inconceivable!

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.060
I refuse to let this self-indulgent,

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.940
unproductive scum who's 
posting complete nonsense

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.020
outdo me, ever!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.850
But, Tonegawa-sensei, this is impossible.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:47.580
If you don't even know what "buzzworthy" 
means, you can't hope to...

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:48.710
Shut up!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.900
I'll just have to learn what I need to know.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.770
I can just do the same thing!

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:57.530
Everything that this hater 
does, to the letter!

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.640
Th-That might be true, but...

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:03.540
Teach me what I need to know to pull it off!

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:06.240
Start with animated gifs of cats!

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:11.550
<i>Tonegawa decides to forsake pride 
and principle to go for the win.</i>

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.550
Let's see...

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.530
This is where you get gifs.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.880
I see.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.180
<i>Not only does he learn where to get gifs,</i>

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:21.220
<i>but in the morning...</i>

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:29.960
<i>Yuinyan-senpai!</i>

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.210
<i>Ruffle my hair, please!</i>

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.700
<i>If you insist.</i>

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.850
<i>Just once, okay?</i>

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:42.170
<i>Here. Ruffle, ruffle.</i>

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:48.840
<i>He records popular anime and 
makes sure to check them all.</i>

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.590
<i>Come on, let's go home, Michiko.</i>

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.150
<i>Call me Mitchy!</i>

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:59.860
<i>It's all just harmless fluff...</i>

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:01.350
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:04.450
<i>I think now I understand what</i>

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.300
<i>the current hot trends are, 
and what gave rise to them.</i>

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.730
Innocence...!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.870
<i>All the weather-related tweeting then ceases!</i>

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.490
Look at this...!

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.390
What are you doing, Tonegawa-sensei?

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:24.870
Can't you tell? I'm taking food pictures.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.000
<b>Who's in this photo?</b>

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.000
Grass for lolling

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.120
That's... not what that means.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:32.130
What do you mean?

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:36.130
<i>Though he makes his fair share of mistakes...</i>

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:53.360
<i>We're always by your side 
here at Teiai Finance.</i>

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.360
TEIAI <b>Finance</b>

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.360
<b><i>Plan responsibly.</i></b>

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.110
Contact Teiai Finance if you're in need of funds!

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.160
<i>And after a few days, he reaches the 
point where he's able to upload video.</i>

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.750
This had me LOLing

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:08.750
Make sure to include all 
the capitals... There.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.000
<i>He even gains a grasp of Internet slang.</i>

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.220
<i>Tonegawa improves at a remarkable pace!</i>

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:17.010
<i>And yet...</i>

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.260
<b>Tweets      Following      Followers</b>

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.510
<b>Tweets      Following      Followers</b>

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.730
Why isn't he losing followers?!

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:25.600
Damn it!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:30.520
<i>I suppose I can't beat him if all 
I'm doing is following his lead!</i>

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:36.610
<i>A rare development for Tonegawa. 
For once, he cannot see a path to victory!</i>

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.030
<i>And before long...</i>

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.170
<i>Honestly! Keiichirou, you're so stupid!</i>

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.410
<i>They're showing! They're showing!</i>

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.210
<i>Shut up! Why can't you just 
ruffle my hair like usual?!</i>

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.360
<i>But... Yuinyan, you said—</i>

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.670
<i>It's not enough! I need more!</i>

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.260
What the hell am I doing?!

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.270
<i>Tonegawa is lost!</i>

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:10.270
<i>And the next day...</i>

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.070
What did you call me down here for, Saemon?

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.900
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.450
Did you see the tweet on the 
hate account this morning?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.160
Not yet... What was it?

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.040
Look here.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:37.920
Bean sprouts are the only thing in the 
Teiai cafeteria miso soup. Good luck
subsisting on bean sprout power, corporate drones!

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:37.920
"Bean sprouts are the only thing 
in the Teiai cafeteria miso soup."

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.980
What's the big deal about 
this nonsensical tweet?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.430
<b>Psst...</b>

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.430
Wait...

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.430
Let me see that miso soup!

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:01.650
Precisely. The specific contents of the soup

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.950
are something that no one 
from the outside could know.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.080
<b>Psst...</b>

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.450
Which means these hate posts...

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.960
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.210
are coming from someone inside the company!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:21.720
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:26.720
<i>The shocking truth is revealed! 
What was thought to be a random scumbag</i>

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:31.730
<i>is now likely a Teiai employee! 
And the likelihood is strong!</i>

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:40.230
<i>The culprit... is someone in this room!</i>

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.610
<i>He can't trust anyone anymore!</i>

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.930
<i>His suspicions will be continued!</i>

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:52.000
<b>Ebi Roll</b>

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:50.890
<i>Next keyword: Ebi roll!</i>

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:57.000
Here comes the foreman!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.000
<b><i>1-Day Excursion
Foreman</i></b>

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.740
<i>The underground prison. 
The absolute bottom of the barrel.</i>

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.760
<i>Teiai's subterranean labor camp.</i>

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.180
<i>Something that isn't common knowledge</i>

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.870
<i>is the special privileges afforded 
to the foreman of each team.</i>

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:19.270
<b>The Foreman Privilege</b>

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:19.270
<i>The Foreman Privilege!</i>

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:21.960
<i>To maintain mental stability</i>

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:26.350
<i>and keep productivity high, 
entertainment concepts are permitted</i>

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:29.420
<i>for the laborers, under the 
responsibility of the foreman.</i>

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:34.050
<i>It is because of this that the 
foreman of Team E, Ootsuki,</i>

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.140
<i>is allowed to gamble, 
which is normally prohibited!</i>

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:42.420
<i>He's permitted to run games of Chinchirorin 
under this special exemption.</i>

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:50.680
This is the foreman of Team E, Ootsuki, 
requesting permission to run a game.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:53.810
<i>All right. Permission granted.</i>

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.200
Thank you very much.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:06.320
<i>All right, time to fleece the sheep once again!</i>

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.590
<i>Where is everybody?</i>

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.910
<i>Isawa and Numakawa are gone, too.</i>

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.520
Foreman!

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:21.710
Numakawa? Where have you been?

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.620
There's big trouble! It's Team C!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.090
What about Team C?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.280
Just come with me!

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.660
Look at this!

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.220
Wh-What is this?!

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.300
What the heck are they doing?

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:50.990
Over there, Foreman!

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.540
They're all looking at...

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.920
Is that...

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.420
A tablet?!

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:13.180
<b>Psst...Psst... Psst...</b>

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:18.430
Ootsuki.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.810
<i>Odagiri!</i>

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:23.450
<i>Do you remember this man?</i>

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.170
<i>The foreman of Team C, Odagiri!</i>

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.970
<i>After launching a new snack 
line called the Hoppy Meal,</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:36.450
<b>Hoppy</b>

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.450
<i>he began to threaten Team E.</i>

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.370
<i>He's the man Ootsuki cannot afford 
to overlook at the moment!</i>

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:41.110
Ootsuki, you're supposed to be 
quiet when in a movie theater.

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:43.010
What do you mean, movie theater?

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:48.830
It ought to be obvious, 
if you just take a look.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.970
I opened up this place with
my foreman privilege.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:56.970
This has been my dream for a while... 
An underground movie theater.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.410
U-Underground movie theater?!

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:00.600
Yep.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.500
I've been saving for a while, 
a bit at a time...

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:08.980
Money for the tablet and for downloading 
the movies when I'm on the surface.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:13.640
From here on, I'm gonna catch up 
and then outdo your chinchiro profits.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.110
Or so I hope!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:22.250
<i>This bastard... I was wondering 
what he was scheming.</i>

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:26.750
<i>He's been building a house of bricks!</i>

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:31.010
<i>Meanwhile, I've... 
I've been in a house of straw!</i>

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:34.450
<i>All I've had to spend on 
running the chinchiro games</i>

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.360
<i>is a few hundred yen for the dice!</i>

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.260
It's 10,000 Perica for admission.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:44.150
You two want to watch <i>Roman Holiday</i>?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.150
<b>Roman Holiday</b>

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:47.530
N-No, we've got a chinchiro game to run...

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:49.650
Oh? Really?

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:52.900
But that guy in the front row...

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:56.120
Uh, what was his name again?

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.910
That's... Isawa!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.610
Yes, that's it, Isawa!

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:08.070
I thought you were taking the 
day off, since he's here.

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:11.920
That idiot! I thought he was 
in the bathroom or something!

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:15.060
<i>Ow! Ow!</i>

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:19.530
<i>Hello.</i>

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:20.950
<i>Gotcha!</i>

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:21.740
<i>You beast!</i>

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.370
<i>I was so worried!</i>

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:25.830
<i>It was perfectly all right!</i>

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:28.690
<i>I'm sorry, I'm sorry. It was just a joke.</i>

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.680
<i>You didn't really hurt your hand.</i>

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:36.700
<i>Ultimately, both Ootsuki and Numakawa 
find themselves standing and watching.</i>

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.960
<i>And...</i>

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.530
<i>When they look around, they see many 
in the crowd who are mesmerized</i>

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:50.870
<i>by this masterpiece!</i>

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.810
So, did you enjoy <i>Roman Holiday</i>?

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.600
Okay, come on in, Yamaki!

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:09.480
Sure, sure, sure! Step on up, everyone.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.480
<b>Psst...</b>

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:15.440
<b>Audrey Hep-bun 3000 perica</b>

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:15.960
We have special red bean buns to celebrate

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:18.990
<b>Roman Holiday
Underground Premiere Special</b>

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:18.120
<i>Roman Holiday</i>'s premiere 
here in the underground!

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:21.990
We call it... the Audrey Hep-bun!

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.990
<b>Audrey Hep-bun</b>

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.240
Bun pun?!

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:26.750
They're 3,000 Perica apiece!

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:29.240
Step right up and get yourself one!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:32.940
I want one!

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:33.820
I'll take two!

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:34.750
Two over here!

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.260
<i>They actually sell out!</i>

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.660
Foreman Odagiri, what's next?

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:46.950
What are you gonna show next?!

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.930
Well, I was going to keep this a secret...

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:54.940
but since this'll be a premiere, 
I'll make an exception.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.190
Next time, we're screening the 
suspenseful jailbreak drama

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:00.780
that had America on the edge of their seats...

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.780
<i>Prison Break</i>!

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.780
<b>Prison
Break
1-5</b>

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.790
Seasons 1 through 5!

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.290
We'll be screening each episode in sequence.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:29.560
O-da-giri! O-da-giri! O-da-giri!

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:21.550
Come back to us, Isawa!

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.560
<i>They're heating up!</i>

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.600
<i>No! You can't show them </i>Prison Break<i>!</i>

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:39.070
<i>If a romantic comedy like 
</i>Roman Holiday<i> was that popular,</i>

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.840
<i>showing a bunch of forced laborers</i>

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:43.820
<i>who live underground a show 
about escaping prison...</i>

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.500
<i>They'll never give my 
chinchiro games a chance!</i>

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.580
<i>And he'll be blown away...</i>

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.960
<i>by the winds generated by 
this white hot anticipation!</i>

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:56.790
Can we watch right now on that tablet?!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.590
No. We're not given 
Internet access down here,

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:04.680
so I'm going to download it 
next time I get a one-day pass.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:08.120
Using free wi-fi spots!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:23.860
Wi-fi! Wi-fi! Wi-fi!

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.610
<i>Can't you idiots pronounce "wi-fi" correctly?!</i>

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.860
<i>And thus, in time...</i>

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:28.870
<i>Odagiri is set free in pursuit of downloads!</i>

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.130
You awake, Odagiri-san?

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.370
Ootsuki! What are you doing here?

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:47.140
Looks like the day of our 
excursions happened to align.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:52.890
Perhaps there's a good reason for it, though...

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:58.270
If you'd like, Odagiri-san, 
maybe after you download your movies...

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:02.650
We could have a few drinks. My treat.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:10.090
<i>I have to shut him down before 
he manages to blow me away.</i>

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:15.670
<i>And this story will abruptly 
end right here for today!</i>

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.870
<i>You'll see the continuation next time!</i>

00:22:55.670 --> 00:22:57.700
<i>Next time, "Conclusions."</i>

00:22:56.620 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Conclusions</b>
